cff-version: 1.2.0

message: "If you use TUNA in your work, please cite the paper listed under preferred-citation."

title: "TUNA: A streamlined quantum chemistry program for atoms and diatomics"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Brough
    given-names: Harry
    email: harry.brough@manchester.ac.uk
    affiliation: "Department of Chemistry, The University of Manchester"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8373-4023"

abstract: >-
  TUNA is an open-source quantum chemistry program for atoms and diatomic
  molecules. It provides energies, geometry optimisations, vibrational
  frequencies, response properties, coordinate scans and ab initio molecular
  dynamics through a command-line interface, with implementations of density
  functional theory, many-body perturbation theory and coupled-cluster theory.

